course: dictionary
lesson: 13569
title: Not paying attention
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Inattentive is a long word, but you can break it into parts. The start in- means not, and attentive means paying attention. So inattentive means not paying attention. «Maya was inattentive in class and missed the teacher's instructions.» Maya was not listening, so she missed what she had to do.
explain: Inattentive can also mean not giving enough care or thought to someone's needs. «The inattentive host forgot to offer us a drink.» The host was not looking after the guests well. The same word fits both meanings, so read the sentence to see which one it means.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The inattentive driver looked at his phone and did not see the red light.» Put in "not paying attention" and the sentence still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Inattentive means not paying attention, not listening or watching carefully.
fact: Inattentive can also mean not giving enough care or thought to someone's needs, as in «an inattentive host».
fact: The word has two parts: in- means not, and attentive means paying attention.
fact: «Inattentively» is the adverb. It tells how someone does something: «She read the sign inattentively and walked past it.»
fact: «Inattention» is the noun: «Inattention in class makes it hard to learn.»
exercise: «Maya was inattentive in class and missed the teacher's instructions.» What does inattentive mean here? | *Not paying attention | Very clever and quick | Happy to help the teacher | Playing outside at break
exercise: «The inattentive host forgot to offer us a drink.» What does inattentive mean in this sentence? | Giving lots of presents | *Not giving enough care to the guests | Speaking very loudly | Listening to every word
exercise: «The guard was inattentive, so the hero sneaked past.» Find and copy the word that tells you the guard was not paying attention. | *inattentive | hero | past | guard
test: Ella says inattentive means not paying attention. Which sentence uses the word correctly? | «The inattentive pupil won the race and cheered.» | «The inattentive pupil asked a question about the lesson.» | «The inattentive pupil read every word carefully.» | *«The inattentive pupil missed the homework instructions.»
test: What is the noun form of inattentive? | attend | attentive | *inattention | inattentively
exam: Read: «The inattentive guard let the thief walk past.» What does inattentive mean here? | Glowing in the dark | Watching very carefully | *Not watching carefully | Very angry
